Statement of modification
-------------------------

1. The upstream Python implementation has been relocated, unmodified, to
   `original/`. It is retained as the parity reference that the Go port is
   tested against and as the source of the golden test vectors under
   `testdata/`. It is not built, published or installed by this repository.

2. The library has been reimplemented in Go. The Go code is an independent
   implementation written against the observable behaviour of the Python
   original; it reproduces that behaviour deliberately, including its edge
   cases, so that the two agree byte-for-byte on prompts and within 1e-4 on
   probabilities.

3. The Go port is inference only. The reinforcement-learning training math in
   the upstream package -- `proper_reward`, `td_lambda_targets` and
   `collate_items` -- has no Go counterpart and is not ported.

4. Several upstream inconsistencies are reproduced on purpose, because
   matching them is the point of a parity port, and several are deliberately
   not reproduced. Both sets are enumerated in `docs/INVARIANTS.md` and
   `PLAN.md`.

Kernels from algo-tensor
------------------------

The native backend's tensor kernels -- the tensor type, the shape and NN
operations, the dot, axpy and GEMM kernels and their Plan 9 assembly -- are
not part of this repository. They are a Go module dependency, used
unmodified:

    algo-tensor - pure-Go tensor kernels and neural-network ops
    module github.com/cwbudde/algo-tensor, version v0.3.1
    Copyright (c) 2026 Christian Budde
    Licensed under the MIT License (the LICENSE file of that module)

algo-tensor took these kernels from go-pocket-tts
(github.com/cwbudde/go-pocket-tts) by way of go-whistle, as its source
files record. Until Backlog B.19 (docs/DECISIONS.md D35), go-laya carried
its own copy, lifted from go-pocket-tts at commit
fa68a5fc6cb02e0a9fc0fd62c573419b3ae0b449 into `internal/runtime/tensor` and
`internal/runtime/ops`; this repository's git history holds it. Two of
go-laya's changes to that copy, `tensor.FromOwned` and the overflow fix in
`Narrow`, went upstream into algo-tensor
(https://github.com/CWBudde/algo-tensor/pull/5) before the switch. No code
of go-pocket-tts or algo-tensor is vendored here any more.

